==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|curator|lang=la||one who has care of a thing, a manager, guardian, trustee}} < {{term|curare||to take care of}} < {{term|cura||care, heed, attention, anxiety, grief}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who [[manage]]s, [[administer]]s or [[organize]]s a [[collection]], either independently or employed by a [[museum]], [[library]], [[archive]] or [[zoo]].

